1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:05,674
One passkey, made through Mera.

2
00:00:05,704 --> 00:00:09,253
Its P-256 key goes into PasskeyRegistry, and Monad's

3
00:00:09,283 --> 00:00:13,115
precompile verifies every signature, so each paid run

4
00:00:13,145 --> 00:00:14,662
comes from a person.

5
00:00:15,342 --> 00:00:17,262
Then the non-account part.

6
00:00:17,292 --> 00:00:20,757
Mera evaluates the passkey's PRF with a purpose salt,

7
00:00:20,787 --> 00:00:26,005
thenar so101 commands, and HKDF turns it into an Ed25519

8
00:00:26,035 --> 00:00:28,919
key, held in a Mera signing session.

9
00:00:28,949 --> 00:00:32,367
Nothing is stored. Derive it again, and it's the same

10
00:00:32,397 --> 00:00:35,524
key; a different purpose gives an independent one.

11
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:39,042
That key signs the commands to the operator's own arm,

12
00:00:39,072 --> 00:00:41,293
and the arm relay obeys only its owner.

13
00:00:42,204 --> 00:00:43,950
No seed phrase, no key file:

14
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:45,528
one passkey, many keys.

